   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend chapter 329 of the laws of 2009, amending the family court act\nand the social services law relating to removing special powers granted to the\nsociety for the prevention of cruelty to children, in relation to the\neffectiveness thereof",
    "basePrintNo": "S7533",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7533-2025",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §14, Chap 329 of 2009",
    "lawSection": "Family Services",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S7533\n\nSPONSOR: HARCKHAM\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend chapter 329 of the laws of 2009, amending the family\ncourt act and the social services law relating to removing special\npowers granted to the society for the prevention of cruelty to children,\nin relation to the effectiveness thereof\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL::\n\nThis bill will extend the operations for the Rockland Society for the\nPrevention of Cruelty to Children for two years until August 11, 2027.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS::\n\nSection 1 of the bill amends chapter 175 of the laws of 2021 to extend\nthe expiration for two years in relation to the Rockland County SPCC\nuntil August 11, 2027.\n\nSection 2 relates to the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION::\n\nIn 2009, the legislature disbanded all Society for the Prevention of\nCruelty of Children (SPCC) organizations in the state except for chap-\nters in Erie and Rockland County. They were exempt from the law because\nthey both operate in a cooperative manner with local governments, Erie\nCounty has since ceased operation as of 2017. This bill recognizes the\ncontinued efforts of. the Rockland County SPCC in assisting local police\ndepartments to prevent underage alcohol and tobacco sales, by providing\na two-year extension so that the County's SPCC, which has provided an\ninvaluable service for many years, may continue to thwart such sales.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY::\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS::\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE::\n\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n",
